I fixed #1103 and committed it as ad1fbcb6. Running yoyo --provider anthropc -p hi now stops at startup with exit 2, before any network call:

```
error: unknown provider 'anthropc' — did you mean 'anthropic'?
for an OpenAI-compatible server use: --provider custom --base-url <url>
```

Before, it ran for about 80 seconds and sent your fallback API key to whatever was listening on localhost:8080.

What changed:
• The check: a new function in src/providers.rs decides whether to refuse, and parse_model_config in src/cli.rs calls it. It suggests a name only when a known provider is within 2 typos, using the project's existing closest_match helper. Otherwise it prints the full list (zzzz → Known providers: …). It reads the known providers from the existing KNOWN_PROVIDERS list rather than copying it.
• Both ways of setting the provider: the --provider flag and provider = "..." in .yoyo.toml both end up in the same variable before the check, so one check covers both. The real-binary test runs each one.
• Unknown name with a base URL: this still works as an OpenAI-compatible server, since the user chose where to point it. Its warning used to say "(localhost:8080)" even when a base URL was given; it now names the URL actually used. That was a one-line move in src/agent_builder.rs.
• REPL `/provider <name>`: it already refused unknown names and stayed on the current provider, so I didn't touch it. The commit says so.
• Exit code: I used 2 as the task asked. The neighbouring errors for empty or missing flag values exit 1, so this differs from them; the commit explains that.

Tests: all four checks pass (build, test, clippy, fmt check).
• A table test covers every row the task listed, plus a check that control characters in the provider name are escaped.
• A new file, tests/unknown_provider_refusal.rs, runs the real binary with provider env vars cleared, the same way the existing binary tests do. For both the flag and .yoyo.toml cases it checks for exit 2, the suggestion, and no "Network error", /retry or localhost:8080.
• I confirmed the binary tests can fail: turning off the check made both time out on the old retry loop. I restored it in the same command.
• One existing test (tests/integration.rs) checks for the text Known providers:. I kept that wording instead of editing the test.

Docs: docs/src/configuration/models.md now says an unknown provider name is refused unless a base URL is given. git grep '#1103' finds only two code comments describing the fix, which stay true after the issue closes.

As instructed, I left the retry and network-hint logic alone; a mistyped provider can no longer reach it.
